      "title": "US carries out another round of ‘minor’ strikes on Iran, Trump says",
      "link": "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/nov/07/us-carries-out-another-round-of-minor-strikes-on-iran-trump-says",
      "description": "<p>The president’s announcement comes days after an earlier attack on Iran was made public, and as diplomatic efforts to end the conflict have accelerated</p><p>Donald Trump has said the US military on Friday carried out a new round of limited strikes on Iran, targeting an air defence system, describing the action as “minor.”</p><p>Iranian state media reported the sound of two explosions in the Suza area of Qeshm Island, which is in the strait of Hormuz, the crucial waterway for oil shipments that has been disrupted since the beginning of the US war on Iran in February.</p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/nov/07/us-carries-out-another-round-of-minor-strikes-on-iran-trump-says\">Continue reading...</a>",
      "source_name": "The Guardian World",
      "published": "2026-11-07T03:07:01"
    },
    {
      "title": "US carries out fresh targeted strikes on Iran's air defences: Trump",
      "link": "https://www.business-standard.com/world-news/us-carries-out-fresh-targeted-strikes-on-iran-s-air-defences-trump-126110700064_1.html",
      "description": "President Donald Trump said the US military on Friday carried out fresh limited strikes on Iran, targeting its air defense systems.\nIranian state media reported the sound of two explosions in the Suza area of Qeshm Island, which is in the crucial waterway for oil shipments.\nTrump in an exchange with reporters described the military action as \"minor\".\n\"They knocked out -- they built a little bit of an anti-aircraft device and we knocked it out in about 15 minutes, maybe five,\" Trump told reporters shortly after arriving in West Palm Beach, Florida, on Friday evening.\nThe US military also reported carrying out what it described as defensive strikes on Monday. Explosions were heard on the islands of Qeshm and Hengam in the strategic Strait of Hormuz, and in the nearby mainland area of Bandar Abbas.\nFriday's strikes are the first since Trump's Republican Party was dealt a stunning repudiation in Tuesday's midterm elections in the US.\nThe electoral setback was stoked in part by voter",
      "source_name": "Business Standard Latest",
      "published": "2026-11-07T02:07:43"
    }
